{"title":"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part D","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that there are no integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe09f9ffebd3bec5ef42ef10048da0c392e79ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{p + q} 5^{p - q} = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can assume that there are integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that the equation is true.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2fc57101c378366401a2f8dc3afb1110ba2f0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{4} \\times 5^{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. The powers on both sides of the equation must be the same, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc95ba3c1aac50767476898e5ef63c85aab59e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2c8a4c75619989b925886858a9e5799a580ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - q = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Adding the equations, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e5bdc84ab1dacfccda42d9fecd1a5026ab59df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c9925c5c9c964c4a3ab50d7516202c1e614310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> must be an even integer. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not even, so we have a contradiction. Thus, there are no integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0b4963c3e5b7f8af2f4deb9fde28c54c5b5734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{p + q} \\times 5^{p - q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can assume that there are integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that the equation is true.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2fc57101c378366401a2f8dc3afb1110ba2f0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{4} \\times 5^{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. The powers on both sides of the equation must be the same, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc95ba3c1aac50767476898e5ef63c85aab59e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2c8a4c75619989b925886858a9e5799a580ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - q = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>From the first equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be both even or both odd since their sum is an even number and both numbers are integers. However, from the second equation, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be odd while the other must be even because both are integers and their sum is an odd number. This leads to a contradiction because both can't be even if one is odd and both can't be odd if one is even.\n</p><p>Thus, we conclude that there are no integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0b4963c3e5b7f8af2f4deb9fde28c54c5b5734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{p + q} \\times 5^{p - q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065744\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 140/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/209